# New target: Synology DSM 7.1, "evansport" platform (32-bit i686), e.g.
# DS214play. Synology never built PHP8.x for i686; 7.4.30-0118 (Oct 2022) is
# the last i686 PHP7.4 build it shipped on package centre.
#
# PKG_VER is intentionally 7.4.30-0009 here, NOT -0118: every i686 .spk from
# -0112 onward (including -0118) is wrapped in Synology's post-2022 package
# code-signing/encryption container ("FA AD BE EF" header, see synacktiv's
# "Extraction of Synology encrypted archives" Pwn2Own Ireland 2024 writeup);
# unpacking it needs Synology's proprietary embedded signing/encryption keys,
# which this project does not attempt to extract. -0009 (same revision as the
# avoton reference) predates that rollout and is still a plain POSIX tar, so
# it is used here purely as a LOCAL BUILD-TIME reference (link-stub libs +
# comparison binary for parity.sh/verify-ext.sh/run-tests.sh). It is
# independent from deploy-evansport-dsm71/target.env's PKG_VER, which must
# instead match whatever PHP7.4 build is actually installed on the real NAS
# (check over SSH) — SONAMEs for the linked libs (pcre2/onig/sybdb) are
# stable across these Synology package revisions, so this split is safe.
#
# HOST confirmed (inspected inside ds.evansport-7.1.dev.txz: usr/local/i686-pc-linux-gnu/).
# PCRE2_VER/ONIG_VER/LIBXML2_VER default to the avoton values; re-verify them
# against the extracted evansport sysroot/package once build/setup-env.sh has
# run (see README "Building from source" for the inspection commands) and
# override below if they differ.
: "${PLATFORM:=evansport}"
: "${DSM_VER:=7.1}"
: "${HOST:=i686-pc-linux-gnu}"
: "${BUILD:=$HOST}"          # override to x86_64-pc-linux-gnu if native i686
                              # execution is unavailable on the build host
: "${PKG_ARCH:=i686}"
: "${PKG_VER:=7.4.30-0009}"
: "${REF_PHP_VER:=7.4.30}"
: "${NEW_PHP_VER:=7.4.33}"
: "${PCRE2_VER:=10.40}"
: "${ONIG_VER:=6.9.5}"
: "${LIBXML2_VER:=2.9.4}"
# build libsybdb (FreeTDS) from source instead of copying the reference
# package's prebuilt one: that prebuilt .so is linked against the DSM6-era
# OpenSSL SONAME (libssl.so.1.0.0), absent from the evansport/DSM7.1
# toolkit's sysroot (which ships OpenSSL 1.1.1n only) -- confirmed by a real
# build+load test in this session. See build-ext-deps.sh.
: "${FREETDS_FROM_SOURCE:=1}"
: "${W:=$HOME/synobuild-evansport}"
